(ct ) are stochastic price sensitive functions. When storage is permitted, for inventory 
carried forward there is a wastage factor d ∈(0,1). This implies that storage of q units at 
time t-1 yields (1 − d )q units of the commodity at time t. 
The spot price, Zt , of the commodity is determined by market clearing. At each 
point in time, there are two sources of supply: production g t  and incoming inventory 
(1−d)Qt−1. There are two sources of demand: consumption c t  and outgoing inventory 
